  "reasoning": "The product contains an isatin (indole-2,3-dione) core with fluoro and iodo substituents on the aromatic ring, along with a carboxylic acid group at position 2. In the context of deprotection reactions, carboxylic acids are routinely masked as esters during synthesis to control reactivity. Based on standard synthetic strategies and the provided examples, the methyl ester is the most common protecting group for such acidic functionalities. Disconnecting the proton of the carboxylic acid reveals the methyl ester precursor. Hydrolysis of this ester under mild acidic or basic conditions would selectively yield the free carboxylic acid without disturbing the halogen substituents or the lactam/lactone carbonyls.",
  "final_answer": "COC(=O)c1c[nH]c2c(F)cc(I)cc2c1=O"
}

